   full colored-fiber reduction above is necessary.
2. The sign cannot be imported from the simple cube. Its positive relative
   edge is a counterexample to that extrapolation, whereas all degree-six
   tori in scope have the opposite leading sign. The \(L=4\) overlap count
   also cannot be borrowed from \(L\ge6\).
3. The variational bump is not an actual prepared state or a selected vacuum.
   Actual-output access is proved separately by positive flat-fiber overlap
   and fixed-vector spectral convergence.
4. No equality of the full-sector and actual cyclic bottoms at each fixed
   nonzero \(g\) is proved. Possible invariant electric/matter components are
   bypassed only at the leading \(g^{-2}\) scale.
5. A prescribed positive first-birth time produces a different, \(g\)-dependent
   incoming state. No uniform statement for such times, unknown-time
   mixture, no-event filtering or full ensemble is established here.
6. The mean in the fixed output is instead exactly
   \(g^2\langle D\rangle/(2\tau)+\langle H_4\rangle/(4\tau g^2)\), with
   its own finite-vector expectation. A support edge does not set that
   expectation or say that most births have an edge energy. The lower
